  "notes_for_editor": "The CTPA expansion in the story is inferred, not stated by either lookout page: it is most likely the Clearwater Timber Protective Association, one of two predecessors that merged in 1966. Cited the cptpa.com home page because its About text is there; a more specific About URL was not located. Idaho Fire Lookouts gives no documented staffing, so none is written. 'Drive-Up' tag on a destroyed site is included but flagged in the story. 'Patrol point 2 miles northwest' meaning is unclear and is stated as listed. Elevation 4,218 ft is in both pages but elevation_m is empty in the record. The record had no events before this run. No photo with a usable licence was found. Fact-check 2026-10-10: predecessor and merged-body names now match cptpa.com (Potlatch Timber Protective Association; Clearwater-Potlatch Timber Protective Association). The 1923 sentence now carries its cite. The story now flags the drive-up tag as possibly out of date for a destroyed site. The CTPA expansion is stated as an unconfirmed inference.",
